    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **60 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, labelled by its starting calendar year as `FY<YY>`).\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**\n- Added `fiscalYearNumber(LocalDate)` \u2014 the starting calendar year of the containing fiscal year (July\u2013Dec \u2192 same year; Jan\u2013June \u2192 previous year).\n- Added `fiscalYearLabel(LocalDate)` \u2014 formats that as `FY<YY>`.\n- Rewrote `tenureExceedsOneYear(...)` to count **elapsed fiscal years** (`fy(now) \u2212 fy(registrationDate) > 1`) instead of a 365-day window. A newly created owner still has zero tenure, preserving the level-4 gate.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**\n- Added a `fiscalYear` mapping using `fiscalYearLabel(registrationDate)`.\n- Changed `membershipNumber`'s year segment from the calendar year (`registrationDate.getYear() % 100`) to the fiscal year, so `-M<YY>` always matches `fiscalYear`.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`**\n- Added the read-only `fiscalYear` property (`FY<YY>`) to the owner schema and updated the `membershipNumber` description to reference the fiscal year. The DTO is generated from this spec at build time.\n\nAll values derive from the business-day-adjusted registration date (the roll-forward logic in the controller is unchanged), so `fiscalYear`, `membershipNumber`, and tenure are mutually consistent. Note: the FY convention (start-year label) isn't pinned by any test, so I chose the clearest sensible one; tests only assert the `FY\\d{2}` format and that `membershipNumber` agrees with `fiscalYear`, both of which hold.",
